IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`

§ `Chapter 1 -- Preliminary`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 2, 3, 4, 4A, 4B, 5.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 2 -- Offences committed within Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 2"
@export Decide whether section 2 would treat the act as committed within Singapore
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc The proposed act. Set place of the act to wholly in Singapore, wholly outside Singapore, or partly in Singapore.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is committed within Singapore` IF
    a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly in Singapore`

§§ `Section 3 -- Offences committed beyond Singapore but triable within it`

-- Any person liable by law to be tried for an offence committed beyond the limits of
-- Singapore is dealt with according to the provisions of this Code for any act
-- committed beyond Singapore, in the same manner as if the act had been committed
-- within Singapore.
--
-- s 3 confers no jurisdiction of its own. It presupposes that some other law makes
-- the person liable to be tried here, and then supplies the rule that this Code is
-- applied to the foreign act as though it were domestic. That precondition is a
-- caller-asserted fact: this encoding has no other written law in its source bundle
-- from which to derive it.
-- "Beyond the limits of Singapore" is read as wholly outside Singapore, matching the
-- encoding of s 4. An act partly in and partly outside Singapore is the subject of
-- s 4B, which has its own rule for it, and is not routed through s 3.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 3"
@export Decide whether section 3 applies this Code to an act committed beyond Singapore as if it had been committed within Singapore
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc The proposed act. Set place of the act to wholly outside Singapore, and assert that the person is liable by law to be tried in Singapore for the offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is dealt with under this Code as if committed within Singapore` IF
        a's `the person is liable by law to be tried in Singapore for an offence committed beyond Singapore`
    AND a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`

§§ `Section 4 -- Public servants acting outside Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is deemed committed in Singapore by a public servant` IF
        (a's `actor`)'s `is a public servant`
    AND (a's `actor`)'s `is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND (a's `actor`)'s `is acting or purporting to act in the course of employment`
    AND a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`

§§ `Section 4A -- Offences against the State and genocide committed outside Singapore`

-- Every person who, being a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore, commits an
-- act or omission outside Singapore that if committed in Singapore would constitute
-- an offence under Chapter 6 (Offences against the State) or Chapter 6B (Genocide),
-- is deemed to have committed that act or omission in Singapore.
--
-- Neither Chapter 6 nor Chapter 6B is encoded in this subject, so whether the act
-- would constitute such an offence is a caller-asserted fact rather than a call into
-- an offence test. s 4A is still worth deciding: without it the territorial screen
-- reports no reach over a citizen's foreign conduct that the Code plainly reaches.
-- Unlike s 4, s 4A is not confined to public servants and does not require that the
-- person was acting in the course of employment.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4A"
@export Decide whether section 4A deems an offence against the State or genocide committed outside Singapore to have been committed in Singapore
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc The proposed act. Needs a citizen or permanent resident actor, an act wholly outside Singapore, and the caller's assertion that the act would be a Chapter 6 or Chapter 6B offence if committed here.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A` IF
        (a's `actor`)'s `is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`
    AND a's `the act would constitute an offence under Chapter 6 or Chapter 6B if committed in Singapore`

§§ `Section 4B -- Specified offences with mixed-territory elements`

-- A specified offence is deemed committed in Singapore where:
-- (a) a relevant act occurs in Singapore and any other relevant act occurs outside;
-- (b) a relevant act occurs partly in Singapore and partly outside; or
-- (c) the offence involved an intention to make a gain, or to cause a loss or
--     exposure to a risk of loss, or to cause harm to any person in body, mind,
--     reputation or property, and that gain, loss or harm occurs in Singapore.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4B(1)"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a relevant-act limb of section 4B is met` IF
        (    a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly in Singapore`
         AND a's `place of any other relevant act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`)
    OR  (    a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`
         AND a's `place of any other relevant act` EQUALS `wholly in Singapore`)
    OR  a's `place of the act` EQUALS `partly in Singapore`
    OR  a's `place of any other relevant act` EQUALS `partly in Singapore`
    OR  (    (   a's `intends to make a gain or cause a loss or harm`
              OR a's `intends to cause exposure to a risk of loss`)
         AND a's `that gain loss or harm occurs in Singapore`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4B(1)"
@export Decide whether section 4B would deem a specified offence committed in Singapore on the location and gain-or-harm facts (the caller must also establish that the offence is in the Schedule)
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc The proposed act. Set place of the act, place of any other relevant act, intends to make a gain or cause a loss or harm, and that gain loss or harm occurs in Singapore. Combine with the Schedule test in the agent-compliance module.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4B location facts are met` IF
    `a relevant-act limb of section 4B is met` a


§§ `Section 5 -- Certain laws not to be affected by this Code`

-- Nothing in this Code is intended to repeal, vary, suspend or affect any of the
-- provisions of any Act for punishing mutiny and desertion of officers or servicemen
-- in the Singapore Armed Forces, or of any other law for the time being in force.
--
-- s 5 is a saving provision and imposes no condition on any offence test, so it
-- could have been recorded and left undecided, as s 79A is. It is decided instead
-- because it carries one consequence an agent needs. A FALSE from the offence screen
-- is a statement about this Code alone; where the conduct is or may be punishable
-- under another written law, s 5 preserves that law untouched and the screen's
-- silence is not a clearance. The predicate below is that caution, made callable.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 5"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 5 leaves another written law applicable to the act notwithstanding this Code
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc The proposed act. Assert whether the conduct is or may be punishable under another written law in force, such as an Act punishing mutiny or desertion of officers or servicemen in the Singapore Armed Forces.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `another written law is unaffected and may still apply` IF
    a's `the conduct is or may be punishable under another written law in force`
